WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.145
Fake audio detectors work well on the data they
were trained on,

00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:08.699
but their accuracy collapses when they meet audio
from a new dataset.

00:00:08.779 --> 00:00:12.594
Fine-tuning on the new data then makes them forget
the old,

00:00:12.674 --> 00:00:15.301
a problem called catastrophic forgetting.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:20.714
This ICML 2023 paper introduces Regularized
Adaptive Weight Modification, or RAWM,

00:00:20.794 --> 00:00:26.655
a continual learning method that adapts how it
modifies network weights based on the ratio

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.635
of genuine to fake utterances,

00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:35.170
and adds a regularization term so the model
remembers the feature distribution of earlier datasets.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.480
Without replaying any past samples,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:43.421
RAWM cuts forgetting to roughly one tenth of naive
fine-tuning and even generalizes beyond

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:47.250
audio to speech emotion recognition and image recognition.
